  "id": "DrugBank_DB00456 - MONDO_4471",
  "verbalization": "Cefalotin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Bacterial Arthritis through a chain of indications that link it to Arthropathy and subsequently to bacterial infection. The evidence suggests that Cefalotin may be associated with Arthropathy, which is a condition that can predispose individuals to bacterial infections, particularly in the joints. This relationship is supported by the shared indication of Arthropathy between Cefalotin and other antibiotics, such as Cephalexin and Cefradine, which are also linked to Bacterial Arthritis. The presence of these indications implies a potential role for Cefalotin in the development of bacterial arthritis, possibly through its effect on inflammatory processes or by influencing the microbiome. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Cefalotin contributes to the development of bacterial arthritis via its interaction with arthropathic conditions.",
